usage: trace_deep_arm_jit_ovmf.py [-h] --efi EFI --kernel KERNEL --device-tree
                                  DEVICE_TREE --output OUTPUT --physical-base
                                  PHYSICAL_BASE --virtual-base VIRTUAL_BASE
                                  --memory-size MEMORY_SIZE --kernel-physical
                                  KERNEL_PHYSICAL --tools TOOLS
                                  [--instruction-budget INSTRUCTION_BUDGET]
                                  [--deep-diagnostic | --tiered-diagnostic]
                                  [--platform-profile {nextcore-irq-compat-v1}]
                                  [--initial-override INITIAL_OVERRIDE]
                                  [--initial-pstate INITIAL_PSTATE]
                                  [--vector-base VECTOR_BASE]
                                  [--irq-level IRQ_LEVEL]
                                  [--fiq-level FIQ_LEVEL]
                                  --allow-incomplete-sptm-prefix [--qemu QEMU]
                                  [--host-memory-mib HOST_MEMORY_MIB]
                                  [--timeout TIMEOUT] [--ovmf-code OVMF_CODE]
                                  [--ovmf-vars OVMF_VARS]

Bounded, opt-in incomplete SPTM prefix diagnostic inside x86 OVMF EFI. This
records an actual fault or instruction-budget return; it does not provide SPTM
services, a platform device tree, authentication, or a macOS boot result.
Original-image addresses and instruction words belong in a private output
path.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --efi EFI
  --kernel KERNEL
  --device-tree DEVICE_TREE
  --output OUTPUT
  --physical-base PHYSICAL_BASE
  --virtual-base VIRTUAL_BASE
  --memory-size MEMORY_SIZE
  --kernel-physical KERNEL_PHYSICAL
  --tools TOOLS         canonical authored OVMF helper directory
  --instruction-budget INSTRUCTION_BUDGET
  --deep-diagnostic     explicitly select only the deep-16384 tier
  --tiered-diagnostic   explicitly require the opt-in tiered EFI build;
                        allows256/1024/4096
  --platform-profile {nextcore-irq-compat-v1}
  --initial-override INITIAL_OVERRIDE
  --initial-pstate INITIAL_PSTATE
  --vector-base VECTOR_BASE
  --irq-level IRQ_LEVEL
  --fiq-level FIQ_LEVEL
  --allow-incomplete-sptm-prefix
  --qemu QEMU
  --host-memory-mib HOST_MEMORY_MIB
  --timeout TIMEOUT
  --ovmf-code OVMF_CODE
  --ovmf-vars OVMF_VARS
